# The signals of chapter 7's flash-stall waveform, for scripts/vcd_wave.py: path, label,
# format, the report's colour for the core or the flash controller, and the states in which
# the value is the one to read. The state names are the two-letter codes of the FSM figure.
# CCLK is the pin as the STARTUPE2 model drives it, marked while it clocks a transaction.
# spiflash.sending, dumped for the marks and not drawn, splits the wait into the command and
# address going out on spiflash_mosi and the word coming in on spiflash_miso. mem_rdata is
# marked only where latch_instr takes it: the core ignores it while the word shifts in.
uut.clk                  clk           grid
cpu.control.state        state         0=FI,1=WI,2=FR,3=EX,4=LD,5=WD,6=ST   0072b2
cpu.pc                   pc            hex                                  0072b2  @FI
cpu.instr                instr         hex                                  0072b2  @FR
uut.mem_rstrb            mem_rstrb     bit                                          @FI
uut.mem_rbusy            mem_rbusy     bit                                          @WI
uut.mem_rdata            mem_rdata     hex                                          @WI&latch_instr
cpu.control.latch_instr  latch_instr   bit                                  0072b2  @WI&latch_instr
uut.spiflash_csn         spiflash_csn  bit                                  cc79a7  @WI
glbl.CCLKO_GLBL          CCLK          bit                                  cc79a7  @WI&mem_rbusy
uut.spiflash_mosi        spiflash_mosi bit                                  cc79a7  @WI&spiflash.sending
uut.spiflash_miso        spiflash_miso bit                                  cc79a7  @WI&mem_rbusy&!spiflash.sending
